# Home / marketing landing — responsive contract

**Apply on every task** that touches `apps/web/src/app/home/**` or `apps/web/src/features/home/**`. Full doc: `docs/HOME_LANDING_RESPONSIVE.md`.

## Single scroll (required)

- The **whole site/page** scrolls once (`html`/`body` or `.home-page`) — **never** a fixed-height section with `overflow: auto|scroll` that creates an inner scrollbar when the viewport shrinks.
- Sections use `height: auto`, `max-height: none`, `overflow: visible`. Clip horizontal bleed only: `overflow-x: clip` on `.home-page` / section if needed.
- Visual stages use `min-height` + fluid sizing, not a fixed `height` that clips content.

## Shared layout with header

- Reuse **`HomeShell`** + **`HOME_SHELL_INNER_X_CLASS`** for header and every landing section so left/right edges align (`max-w-[1600px]`, same outer/inner padding).
- Header over hero: `HomeNavigation overlay` + `--home-header-clearance` top padding on hero content (not a white bar pushing hero down).

## Breakpoints (hero & new sections)

| Range | Layout |
|-------|--------|
| **&lt; 640px** | Single column; full-width CTAs; phone-tuned flag/illustration positions |
| **640–767px** | Single column, larger type/visual; CTAs row + wrap |
| **768–1023px** | Two columns (copy \| visual) where the design is side-by-side |
| **≥ 1024px** | Desktop grid per Figma |

Use `clamp()`, `%`, and `minmax()` — not desktop-only px absolutes from Figma.

## CSS cascade (flags / overlays)

- **Base styles** = shared only (position, radius, z-index).
- **Mobile/tablet** positions live in `@media (max-width: …)` blocks.
- **Desktop** positions **only** inside `@media (min-width: 1024px)` — never after mobile queries, or mobile changes will not apply.

## Figma workflow

- Read frame via MCP; implement responsive layout first, then pixel-tune per breakpoint.
- Assets in `public/home/` (no hotlinked Figma URLs).
- See also `09-figma-design.mdc`.
